      "answer_result": "## Comparison and best configuration\n\nThe evidence is a **synthetic Phase 3 fixture, not published research**. It reports Model A: 2.5M params, mIoU 73.27; Model B: 3.2M params, mIoU 76.0; Model C: 2.0M params, mIoU 70.0 [paper_1.pdf, p.1], [paper_2.pdf, p.1], [paper_3.pdf, p.1]. The fixture labels A as convolutional segmentation, B as attention segmentation, and C as a compact convolution baseline; all use the same fixture benchmark/evaluation protocol [paper_1.pdf, p.1], [paper_2.pdf, p.1], [paper_3.pdf, p.1]. It states A improves over C by 3.27 points at 0.5M more params, and B improves over A by 2.73 points at 0.7M more params [paper_1.pdf, p.1], [paper_2.pdf, p.1], [paper_3.pdf, p.1]. Claims are descriptive quality/cost tradeoff only; no causal or ablation claim and no uncertainty estimates are reported [paper_1.pdf, p.1], [paper_2.pdf, p.1], [paper_3.pdf, p.1].\n\n`experiment.xlsx` is 3 rows × 3 columns (`model`, `params_m`, `miou`) with no missing values; its sample is A = 2.5M/73.27, B = 3.2M/76.0, C = 2.0M/70.0 [Analysis af3903c7-a24e-416c-ab49-bcaa84703b03], [Analysis 88faef1d-07be-4472-b83f-7fae1197c8b9], [Analysis 5630ded8-30ff-4cd2-99b8-7b773feef17f].\n\nComputed output ranks by mIoU: B 76.00 > A 73.27 > C 70.00 [Analysis 2b296c03-333b-463b-bcca-96eaf0ae0bb2], [Analysis 5630ded8-30ff-4cd2-99b8-7b773feef17f]. Best under 3M parameters is **Model A** (2.5M, mIoU 73.27); B is excluded because it is over budget at 3.2M [Analysis 2b296c03-333b-463b-bcca-96eaf0ae0bb2], [Analysis 5630ded8-30ff-4cd2-99b8-7b773feef17f]. Among sub-3M models, C has higher computed mIoU-per-million (35.000 vs 29.308 for A), while A is more accurate [Analysis 5630ded8-30ff-4cd2-99b8-7b773feef17f]. Computed Pearson correlation between `params_m` and `miou` is 0.9891; linear trend slope/intercept is 4.9294/60.4380 [Analysis 2b296c03-333b-463b-bcca-96eaf0ae0bb2]. Computed output reports `comparison.png` and `summary.json` saved [Analysis 2b296c03-333b-463b-bcca-96eaf0ae0bb2], [Analysis 5630ded8-30ff-4cd2-99b8-7b773feef17f].\n\n## Do results support reported design advantages?\n\nNumerically, yes for the descriptive tradeoff: spreadsheet values match the synthetic fixture values, including A over C and B over A differences [paper_1.pdf, p.1], [paper_2.pdf, p.1], [paper_3.pdf, p.1], [Analysis 5630ded8-30ff-4cd2-99b8-7b773feef17f]. This does **not** establish that architecture/design caused the improvements: the sources explicitly claim no causal or ablation claim and report no uncertainty estimates [paper_1.pdf, p.1], [paper_2.pdf, p.1], [paper_3.pdf, p.1]. With n=3 and no uncertainty estimates, significance/uncertainty cannot be assessed from these excerpts [Analysis 2b296c03-333b-463b-bcca-96eaf0ae0bb2], [Analysis 5630ded8-30ff-4cd2-99b8-7b773feef17f]. The provided excerpts do not support causal design claims.",
